# Everything in this workspace that is SHIPPED TO THE BOX must be LF, whatever the
# checkout's `core.autocrlf` would otherwise do on Windows. This is not tidiness:
#
#  - `deploy/ci-deploy.sh` is the forced command sshd runs. A CRLF copy dies on the box
#    with `$'\r': command not found`, which is why deploy/README.md's install one-liner
#    pipes it through `tr -d '\r'` — a step that is easy to forget and whose failure looks
#    like a broken script rather than a broken checkout.
#  - `caddy/Caddyfile`, `docker-compose.yml`, `Dockerfile` and everything under
#    `monitoring/` are read by containers, where a stray `\r` lands inside a value rather
#    than being ignored (a scrape target of "matchsvc:8788\r" resolves to nothing).
#
# Declaring it here means the working tree itself holds LF, so shipping by scp/rsync is as
# correct as shipping through CI's Linux checkout.
deploy/ci-deploy.sh text eol=lf
caddy/Caddyfile     text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml  text eol=lf
Dockerfile          text eol=lf
monitoring/**       text eol=lf
